{# Decision template: will word of how one of the player's quests ended get out? (ADR-001, "Quest endings")
   One request per quest the player finishes, unless quests.ini says always or never for it, sent
   by Quests.cpp. `heard` must reach quests.heard (0.5) for the ending to become a rumour; `far`
   sets how far it travels, as notability 0.5 + 0.4 x far (0.5 to 0.9).

   The quest is its name and type ("Waking Nightmare (a Daedric quest)"); the type tells guild and
   Brotherhood work from the rest. The journal is the first entry the player had and the one the
   journal shows at the end, with the game's alias tags filled in; when the ending restates the
   first entry, as many do, it is the ending alone.

   Calibrated with tools/quest_panel.py on 60 vanilla endings, each labelled as news across Skyrim
   (8), talked of where it happened (20), private (20) or a judgement call (12) (2026-11-21):
     Jev 1.14   heard >= 0.5 tells all 8 wide and all 20 local endings and 2 of the 20 private
                ones (the Ebony Warrior defeated 0.82, defending Sinding 0.58); every other private
                ending reads 0.47 or less, the Thieves Guild's work 0.16 to 0.35. Waking Nightmare
                0.55 to 0.62 by its ending. far: wide 0.71 on average, local 0.35, private 0.26.
                Leaving out the type let 8 private endings through at 0.4 instead of 3.
     d3:4b      about 0.6: all 8 wide, 16 local and 5 private (it takes becoming the Thieves
                Guild's master for news, 0.73).
     Kev-4B     (kev:4b-q8_0) squeezes every answer into 0.2 to 0.65; about 0.45, poorly: at 0.5
                it tells 5 wide, 8 local and 1 private ending, at 0.4 11 private ones.

   Context: quest_text, journal_text. A criterion is exactly one line. #}
[ state setting ]
{{ render_template("submodules\\system_head\\0010_setting") }}
[ end state ]

[ state quest ]
{{ quest_text }}
[ end state ]

[ state journal ]
{{ journal_text }}
[ end state ]

[ question heard noul ]
`journal` is the player's own record of `quest`: how it began and how it ended. Will word of how it ended get out beyond the people who took part, so that ordinary folk around there talk about it?
[ criteria ]
true: Yes: it happened in the open, changed something people can see, or those involved will tell of it.
false: No: it stays with the people who took part, or is kept secret.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question far noul ]
`journal` is the player's own record of `quest`: how it began and how it ended. Will people in other holds of Skyrim hear how it ended and talk about it too?
[ criteria ]
true: Yes: it is news well beyond the hold where it happened.
false: No: if anyone talks of it, it is only near where it happened.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
